#
# Counter-example: a math:CochainComplex declaring no math:cochainCoboundary. A cochain
# complex is defined by its coboundary operator; one naming none is ill-formed. It fires
# the derived qualified-min-count frame (shacl.QualifiedMinCountConstraintComponent →
# math:IncompleteCochainComplex) and NO other finding: it carries no cells, so no
# co-diamond constraint targets it.

@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/cochain-no-coboundary/> .

ex:cochain a math:CochainComplex .
